    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "394dc214-e2ad-4605-ab3f-2c6b83063ef6",
      "text": "Search results",
      "udi": "umb://element/e318a2f861c84c61845af5b09f044654"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "text": {
        "markup": "<p>The search results component can be added to any page where you want the user to be able to search the Q&amp;A content accessible on<span>&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.thepensionsregulator.gov.uk/faq-landing-page\" class=\"govuk-link\">The Pensions Regulator website</a>. Currently this is focused on Q&amp;As for Automatic Enrolment.</p>\n<p>The title and footer links can be overridden. Footer links will always contain a<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>'Show more questions'</strong><span> link, that will show the remaining three questions, two are shown when the page loads. The heading level of the title and its CSS class can be configured via the settings properties</span></p>\n<p>This component should be accompanied with a link, styled as a button that takes the user to the search results component on the page.</p>\n<p>The link requires the following</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the CSS class 'tpr-search-results-nav-button'</li>\n<li>a span tag inside the link value to inform screen readers that this link will open in a new tab (only if JavaScript is disabled)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The JavaScript file<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>'tpr-search-results.js'</strong><span>&nbsp;is provided as part of the&nbsp;</span><strong>'ThePensionsRegulator.Frontend'</strong><span> nuget package. This will need to be included in any view that uses this component.</span></p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "udi": "umb://element/dde55b0fb5114956a211166d73b921a8"
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "650d7119-e9cf-4c26-a08c-21cf2ffbbbbc",
